# 1️⃣ Traversing a Linked List

## 📖 Definition

Traversal means visiting every node of the Linked List exactly once.

---

### Visualization

```
Head

↓

10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → NULL
```

Traversal Output

```
10 20 30 40
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void display(Node* head)
{
    Node* temp = head;

    while(temp != NULL)
    {
        cout << temp->data << " ";
        temp = temp->next;
    }
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

---

# 2️⃣ Searching in a Linked List

## 📖 Definition

Searching means finding whether a particular value exists in the list.

---

### Example

```
10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → NULL

Search = 30
```

Output

```
Found
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool search(Node* head, int key)
{
    while(head != NULL)
    {
        if(head->data == key)
            return true;

        head = head->next;
    }

    return false;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

---

# 3️⃣ Insertion at Beginning

## 📖 Steps

Step 1

Create new node.

↓

Step 2

Point new node to Head.

↓

Step 3

Move Head to new node.

---

### Visualization

Before

```
Head

↓

20 → 30 → NULL
```

Insert

```
10
```

After

```
Head

↓

10 → 20 → 30 → NULL
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void insertAtBeginning(Node* &head, int value)
{
    Node* newNode = new Node();

    newNode->data = value;

    newNode->next = head;

    head = newNode;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(1)
```

---

# 4️⃣ Insertion at End

## 📖 Steps

Move to the last node.

↓

Create new node.

↓

Last node points to new node.

---

### Visualization

Before

```
10 → 20 → NULL
```

Insert

```
30
```

After

```
10 → 20 → 30 → NULL
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void insertAtEnd(Node* &head, int value)
{
    Node* newNode = new Node();

    newNode->data = value;

    newNode->next = NULL;

    if(head == NULL)
    {
        head = newNode;
        return;
    }

    Node* temp = head;

    while(temp->next != NULL)
        temp = temp->next;

    temp->next = newNode;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

