# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Traversal always starts from the Head.

✅ Keep track of the previous node during insertion and deletion.

✅ Handle edge cases like an empty list and a single-node list.

✅ Update the Head pointer when modifying the first node.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Forgetting to update pointers.

❌ Memory leaks due to missing `delete`.

❌ Dereferencing NULL pointers.

❌ Incorrect position handling.

❌ Losing the Head pointer.

---

# 📝 Summary

- Traversal visits every node.
- Searching requires sequential traversal.
- Insertion can be performed at the beginning, end, or any position.
- Deletion requires careful pointer updates.
- Most Linked List operations have **O(n)** complexity, except insertion and deletion at the beginning.

